  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the sum of the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{81}-\u22ef+\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(1/3)^{n}}{n}+\u22ef=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that we can rewrite the given sum as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{81}-\u22ef+\\frac{(1/3)^{n}}{n}+\u22ef= \\\\ (\\frac{1}{3})-\\frac{(1/3)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(1/3)^{3}}{3}-\u22ef+\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(1/3)^{n}}{n}+\u22ef & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{3}) & =(\\frac{1}{3})-\\frac{(1/3)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(1/3)^{3}}{3}-\u22ef+\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(1/3)^{n}}{n}+\u22ef \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{4}{3}) & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{81}-\u22ef+\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(1/3)^{n}}{n}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{4}{3}).$",
